## Authentication Flow

```java
// ✅ JWT validation at Gateway
@Component
public class JwtAuthenticationFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {
    @Override
    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest request, 
                                     HttpServletResponse response,
                                     FilterChain chain) {
        String token = extractToken(request);
        if (token != null) {
            Claims claims = jwtValidator.validate(token);
            
            SecurityContext context = SecurityContextHolder.createEmptyContext();
            context.setAuthentication(new JwtAuthentication(
                UserId.of(claims.getSubject()),
                TenantId.of(claims.get("tenant_id", String.class)),
                extractPermissions(claims)
            ));
            SecurityContextHolder.setContext(context);
            
            // Propagate to downstream services via headers
            request.setAttribute("X-User-ID", claims.getSubject());
            request.setAttribute("X-Tenant-ID", claims.get("tenant_id"));
        }
        chain.doFilter(request, response);
    }
}
```

## Authorization

```java
// ✅ Method-level authorization
@PreAuthorize("hasPermission(#pipelineId, 'pipeline', 'read')")
public Pipeline getPipeline(PipelineId pipelineId) { ... }

@PreAuthorize("hasPermission(#pipelineId, 'pipeline', 'write')")
public Pipeline updatePipeline(PipelineId pipelineId, UpdateCommand cmd) { ... }

@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
public void deleteTenant(TenantId tenantId) { ... }

// ✅ Custom permission evaluator
@Component
public class PravahPermissionEvaluator implements PermissionEvaluator {
    @Override
    public boolean hasPermission(Authentication auth, Object target, Object permission) {
        JwtAuthentication jwt = (JwtAuthentication) auth;
        String perm = target + ":" + permission;  // e.g., "pipeline:write"
        return jwt.getPermissions().contains(perm);
    }
}
```

## Multi-Tenancy Security

```java
// ✅ Tenant context MUST be set before any data access
@Aspect
@Component
public class TenantContextAspect {
    @Before("@annotation(Transactional)")
    public void setTenantContext() {
        TenantId tenantId = SecurityContextHolder.getContext()
            .getAuthentication()
            .getTenantId();
        
        if (tenantId == null) {
            throw new SecurityException("Tenant context required");
        }
        
        // Set for RLS
        jdbcTemplate.execute(
            "SET LOCAL app.current_tenant_id = '" + tenantId.value() + "'"
        );
    }
}

// ❌ NEVER trust client-provided tenant ID
// The tenant ALWAYS comes from the JWT, never from request body/params
```

## Secret Management

```java
// ✅ Secrets from Vault, never hardcoded
@Configuration
public class DatabaseConfig {
    @Value("${spring.datasource.url}")
    private String url;
    
    // Credentials from Vault dynamic secrets
    @VaultPropertySource("database/creds/pipeline-service")
    @Value("${username}")
    private String username;
    
    @Value("${password}")
    private String password;
}

// ❌ NEVER do this
private static final String DB_PASSWORD = "secret123";
private String apiKey = "sk-1234567890";
```

## Security Checklist

Every endpoint MUST:
- [ ] Validate JWT signature and expiry
- [ ] Extract tenant from token (not request)
- [ ] Check permissions before data access
- [ ] Set RLS context before queries
- [ ] Log security events (login, permission denied)
- [ ] Rate limit by tenant/user

Never:
- ❌ Trust client-provided IDs for authorization
- ❌ Hardcode secrets
- ❌ Log sensitive data (tokens, passwords)
- ❌ Return stack traces to clients
- ❌ Use SQL string concatenation
